{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Run-scoped pause/stop/resume for plan autonomy. pause/stop records a request observed only at safe model/tool boundaries; it never kills a provider call or tool. pause leaves the item scheduler-held until explicit resume or human re-acceptance; stop leaves a resumable stopped checkpoint and scheduler hold. resume journals optional guidance and clears the hold, then: when PLAN_AUTONOMY is on and the plan worker is alive it HANDS OFF (2026-11) - stamps a `resume` receipt {run_id, note, time, state:queued} on the item (which un-parks it in the worker) and returns at once with action `queued`; the worker runs the next turn through the normal gate. Running the turn on the request thread used to overlap worker turns, and two runs alternated on one item. With autonomy off (or the worker dead) resume runs the turn itself through step_item, whose plan step lock refuses any overlap with action `busy`. A queued resume of an item that has used its MAX_PLAN_STEPS returns needs_reapproval. It refuses unrelated or still-live runs. Existing verification/lifecycle/completion gates remain authoritative.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;","params":[{"name":"run_id","type":"String"},{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"action","type":"String"},{"name":"note","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"syhhtm1a172795455j611","readers":[],"time":1793907531091,"username":"system","writers":[]}